# Raw data pulls (large; regenerate with data-pipeline scripts)
data/raw/
*.zip

# De-identified usage telemetry (local only — publish only the k-anonymized rollup)
data/usage/

# Filled partner-feedback logs (candid notes stay private; template is tracked)
feedback/

# OSRM routing graphs + OSM extracts (rebuild with deploy/osrm/prepare.sh)
deploy/osrm/foot/
deploy/osrm/car/
deploy/osrm/*.osm.pbf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
*.egg-info/

# Verified sensitive-facility seed lists (handle deliberately; keep only the template)
data-pipeline/seeds/*.csv
!data-pipeline/seeds/template.csv
# The candidates README documents the same unverified lists and, unavoidably,
# names local organizations and the calls made about them — including that a
# named clinic is a crisis pregnancy center rather than a reproductive-health
# provider. That judgment is correct and necessary for routing users safely, but
# publishing it from this repo turns an internal data-quality note into a public
# statement about a named local organization. Keep it local with the CSVs it
# documents; publish deliberately, if ever, not via `git add -A`.
data-pipeline/seeds/CANDIDATES-README.md

# Private outreach repo, cloned in place (github.com/upstateph/upstate-access-outreach).
# Its own git history lives inside; this repo must never see or track its contents.
outreach/

# Personal planning docs — contain personal-network details; keep local only.
# Vestigial now (moved into outreach/), kept as a guard against re-creation here.
outreach-letters-full-set.md
project-context.md

# Secrets / API keys
.env
*.key
census_api_key.txt

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Node (dashboard tooling, if any)
node_modules/

# Keep processed outputs tracked (small JSON the dashboard reads),
# but ignore any scratch exports
data/processed/*.tmp

# Build artifacts
dist/
deploy/artifact.html
deploy/lite/artifact.html
deploy/artifact-access.html
advocacy/briefs/
advocacy/send-packet-partners.md
